// FRONTEND-1 (the Agent mode wire, stacked on FRONTEND-2's #607, the Agent build shell, which is new files only and mounts nothing): the Studio mounts Agent build. Flags: NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENT_MODE AND NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_V4_SHELL, each only the exact string "true"
// (#607's own constant STUDIO_AGENT_MODE_ENABLED in lib/studio-agent-mode.ts, reused; no new flag, so NO .env.example block of this change: the flag's block is #607's). Off (either one), the page mounts nothing, the socket hook routes nothing and sends nothing,
// and every frame and every byte of output is what the base produced.
//   - the socket hook (hooks/use-deckster-websocket-v2.ts): the six agent frames go to the page's run card, ahead of the allowlist (onAgentFrame); the person's card answer goes out as the contract's { type: 'agent_answer', data: { run_id, card, choice } }
//     on the live socket only (sendAgentAnswer: never queued, never replayed); the optional build_mode key rides a user message;
//   - the Builder page (app/builder/page.tsx): the picker above the composer, the cards in the chat after the messages, the run card's state (#607's reducer), the build mode on the four build sends (a ref read at send time), the plan the signed-in session carries (null keeps Agent disabled);
//   - the pure half (lib/studio-agent-mode-wire.ts, new): the page's reducer, when the picker is off, the one rule of an answer, the words of a failed send, the key that brings a card into view.
//   - NO AGENT START FROM VOICE (PK ruling, 11 Nov): a send that comes from the voice call (its two handlers on the page: handleSendMessage for words, handleActionClick for a card's button, a spoken yes to the plan) never carries build_mode "agent". The page asks at the top of each
//     handler whether the words are the ones the call armed (voiceOriginatedSend) and reads the voice build mode (voiceBuildMode: "standard" for a plan that can hold Director's sticky Agent opt-in, else no key) instead of the picker's; the hook turns "agent" on a user message
//     marked mode "voice" into "standard" (last line). Same pattern: marked pure insertions, [has, was] pairs; with the flags off none of it acts.
//   - STANDARD IS SAID OUT LOUD (PK ruling, 12 Nov: "both yes"): Director's Agent opt-in is sticky (saved with the session; only an explicit "standard" clears it) and Studio does not read it back, so after a reload a typed send or a click with the picker on Standard (the key was left out)
//     could still run Agent. On a plan that can hold the opt-in (Pro, Max) a build send with the picker on Standard now carries build_mode "standard" (typedBuildMode, one marked line: the ref the four build sends read); the other plans and the flags off: no key, as today.
//   - RESET TO STANDARD (PK ruling, 12 Nov): when an Agent run finishes the picker goes back to Standard (agentFinishedRun / agentPickerAfterRun in the pure lib, one marked effect on the page and one marked ref). "Finishes" is the reducer's terminal states, done and failed (a refusal
//     before admission is a failed run); "stopped" is not over (the run can be resumed) and does not count. Once, on the move to a finished run: never on mount, never again for the same finished run, and a pick made afterwards stays. The next send on Pro and Max then says "standard"
//     (typedBuildMode), which clears the opt-in Director holds. The first message of a session already carries the picker's mode: it is the typed send of handleSendMessage's unsaved-session branch, one of the four sends that read the ref (nothing to add; the proof pins it).
// Every line this change adds to an EXISTING file carries the marker AGENT-MODE-WIRE (matched as a whole token). In the hook and the Builder page all of them are pure insertions: NO base line is rewritten (older proofs hold every base line of the page and the hook, in order), so the strip
// is a list of [has, was] pairs with was = '': putting each pair back gives the file at STACK_BASE (#607's head) byte for byte. The new files (a lib, this strip, a proof) have no base text.
//   - #607's OWN files, edited in place (PK ruling, 11 Nov: the A1 estimate card is information, not a gate, because the Agent send is the spend click; FRONTEND-2, #607's owner, OK'd the substance): lib/studio-agent-mode.ts (the words), the estimate card, the run cards' mount, the shared button's
//     comment (AGENT_MODE_WIRE_SHELL_EDITS), and #607's own proof (its pairs are in AGENT_MODE_WIRE_PIN_EDITS). The same rule, read strictly: every changed or added line carries the marker (a trailing comment; a JSX comment after a JSX child; in the proof the registry-read mark, which holds it),
//     a line that went leaves a marked comment line in its place, a block that became fewer or more lines is one pair, and the strip puts #607's head back BYTE FOR BYTE (the proof checks exactly that, for every one of these files).
// Older proofs this change teaches (tests only, every line carries the registry-read mark): the two that read the first-parent commits of BASE..HEAD for their own commits' subjects get one more inserted line each, "Agent mode wire:", right after the shell's; two more, ONE marked pure insertion each (gate NEW 1, 12 Nov): the font-selection proof's frame-builder sandbox (scripts/test-theme-font-selection.mjs) defines STUDIO_AGENT_MODE_ENABLED, off (the hook's voice guard names it free there), and chat-theme-export (scripts/test-studio-chat-theme-export.mjs) reads
// that line out of the added-lines budget it holds the font-selection proof to (5, used up on dev) with one splice line; and #607's own proof (above), whose
// scope check held the hook and the Builder page to the base byte for byte ("the drafts are not applied": the one line that applies them now reads them past the later changes' strips, so it is a REPLACED line, a pair like the rest). How the older pins reach it: it REGISTERS its files and its strip
// (scripts/studio-later-changes.mjs, two lines: the env-block list gets none, this change adds no block).
// Plain node, no imports, nothing read from disk or git here.

